    <edge source="instruction" target="bbox_px">
      <data key="d7">95.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The entity described is the instruction to click a specific menu item, which is related to its bounding box coordinates. The bounding box coordinates [214, 128, 374, 181] define the area where the user should click to perform the action. This action involves locating the menu item labeled "Beauty &amp; Personal Care" and clicking it. The bounding box coordinates provide precise pixel locations for the click, ensuring accuracy in identifying the correct menu item. Additionally, there are other instructions related to clicking on bounding boxes for links and buttons located at specific coordinates. These instructions aim to provide accessibility guidance and ensure that users can accurately perform the required actions by clicking on the designated areas.&lt;SEP&gt;To perform the action of clicking a menu item&lt;SEP&gt;The instruction involves bounding box coordinates for the click action.&lt;SEP&gt;The instruction to click the pixel coordinates.&lt;SEP&gt;The instruction to click the bounding box.&lt;SEP&gt;Action performed on bounding box&lt;SEP&gt;The instruction to click the menu item 'Video Games' is related to its bounding box coordinates.</data>
