    <edge source="name" target="bbox_px">
      <data key="d7">126.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The entity referred to as `(bbox_px, name)` is described through various attributes and coordinates. The name of the button corresponds to its bounding box, indicating that the button's label is derived from its location on the screen. For instance, the button labeled "Create an Account" is located at coordinates [1141, 10, 1260, 29]. Similarly, the combobox named "Search entire store here..." is situated at [962, 71, 1212, 103]. Additionally, there is a link named "My Account," which also has a bounding box associated with it. The term "name" is used interchangeably with "bbox_px," suggesting that the name of the element is directly linked to its pixel coordinates. The descriptions emphasize the importance of accessibility, noting that the entity is intended to provide instructions and fulfill roles related to accessibility.&lt;SEP&gt;To perform the action of clicking&lt;SEP&gt;click the link 'Advanced Search'&lt;SEP&gt;The name to click the bounding box.&lt;SEP&gt;Action performed on name and bounding box&lt;SEP&gt;Action performed on bounding box and name&lt;SEP&gt;The name of the menu item 'Video Games' is related to its bounding box coordinates.</data>
